  partName: Intake Manifold
  description: The Intake Manifold is a small, thin-flat component located at the
    middle-center-rear of the engine, responsible for distributing air-fuel mixture
    to the combustion chamber. Its accent yellow color indicates a specialized material
    or coating, which is likely designed to enhance the manifold's durability or
    performance. Notably, the intake manifold's design is critical for ensuring proper
    air-fuel mixture distribution, which directly affects the engine's power output,
    fuel efficiency, and overall performance.
